From 5833674cf816ba403c4c93098d3a3142f50118fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:15:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/46] Fix Discord presence never appearing

Two problems, and the first is why nothing showed at all.

I never ported the play/pause hook from the donor fork. Presence was only
pushed when currentSong emitted, which happens on track change - so signing
in while music was already playing, or pressing play on an already loaded
track, pushed nothing, and pausing never cleared it. onEvents now handles
EVENT_IS_PLAYING_CHANGED: push on resume, which also re-anchors the
progress bar to the real position, and stop the activity on a pause that
isn't just the gap between tracks.

Second, in Kizzy, coroutineContext was declared with a get(), handing out a
fresh SupervisorJob on every access. The job close() cancelled was
therefore never the job the connection ran under, so cancelling it reached
nothing: sockets and heartbeats leaked, and a stale connection could keep
answering isRpcRunning() after logout. It is now built once. close() uses
cancelChildren rather than cancel, since cancelling the scope's own job
would leave it permanently dead and a later connect() would launch into a
cancelled scope - leaving sendActivity spinning forever on a connection
that could never come.

