From e989327818aa23fe2d413857f472822ca0915b21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 11:08:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/46] Fix the presence progress bar sticking at zero, and
 link the artist

Two causes for the stuck bar.

currentSong is database.song(id), so skipping to a track whose row has not
been written yet emits a transient null. The collector treated that as
"stop" and called closeRPC, tearing down the whole gateway on every skip -
so the presence went stale while the socket reconnected. Nulls are now
ignored; pause and stop are handled in onEvents, which is where they
belong.

SongEntity.duration is in seconds and defaults to -1 when unknown, which is
common for a freshly inserted track. That produced an end timestamp earlier
than the start, and Discord renders that as a bar pinned at zero. When the
duration is not known the end timestamp is now omitted entirely, so Discord
shows elapsed time counting up instead.

Also: the artist line is now clickable, opening the artist on YouTube
Music. Discord exposes exactly two url slots, details_url and state_url;
the title already used the first, so the artist takes the second. Local
artists have a generated id that resolves to nothing and stay plain text.
The album cannot be linked - it lives in largeText, which is hover text
with no url slot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019qFVKGXMsRYppSVGRXPgBQ
