From 848bcf59a3960528ac5579eba4bec80242b9b5cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 08:21:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/46] Fix the Discord presence freezing on a track change

Two writers were publishing presences: a collector on currentSong and the
play/pause hook in onEvents. On a skip both fired, and whichever finished
its network round trip last won - so the card often ended up describing
the outgoing track, with an elapsed time from that track against the new
one's length. That is the "2:22/:22" reading.

Worse, the currentSong collector required playbackState == STATE_READY a
full second after the change, and a track change usually spends that
moment BUFFERING. When the guard rejected it nothing retried, so the
presence stayed frozen until something else happened to push an update -
which is why rewinding fixed it and skipping did not: rewinding settles
the player before the check, a skip does not.

There is now one writer. Everything that could change the card requests
an update; a single collector serves those requests, reads what to
publish from the player itself rather than from currentSong (which lags
