From 1873a96e24954e3615b26721bfe834dde086839e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 08:49:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/46] Add app icon customisation

Six launcher icons to choose from, declared as activity-aliases and
switched by enabling one and disabling the rest - Android has no API for
setting an app's icon, so this is the only route there is.

The picker rebuilds each icon from its background colour and foreground
layer rather than drawing @mipmap/ic_launcher, because that resource is
an <adaptive-icon>: a composition the launcher performs, not a drawable
Compose can render.

Also a "use my own image" option, which pins a home screen tile carrying
any picture. A gallery image genuinely cannot become the launcher icon -
icons are compiled resources - and a pinned shortcut is the one place
the system accepts a runtime bitmap. The screen says so plainly instead
of leaving people wondering why the app drawer did not change.

The alias class names are built from MainActivity's package rather than
from context.packageName, since debug builds carry an applicationIdSuffix
that the class names do not, and using the wrong one would have made
every switch silently do nothing on those builds.
