From 5d549d06c7a742efa2997fd9e7aafc59dc1bc582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 10:08:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/46] Add song recognition

A microphone button beside the search field records about twelve seconds,
computes a Shazam-compatible fingerprint on the device, and asks Shazam
what it was. Only the fingerprint is sent - the recording never leaves the
phone and is never written to disk.

Ported from Metrolist, which took it from Aleksey Saenko's MusicRecognizer;
the fingerprint algorithm itself is a port of vibra/SongRec. The shazamkit
module is a plain JVM library like the other siblings here, so its Timber
logging became a small internal logger rather than pulling in a dependency,
and it uses the OkHttp ktor engine that this project already ships instead
of CIO.

android.util.Log does not take format arguments the way Timber does, so
calls like Log.d(TAG, "%d bytes", size) would not have compiled at all.
RecogLog keeps the original call shape and formats only when the line will
actually be printed.

A result opens the existing search rather than playing anything: Shazam
answers with a title and an artist, not a YouTube Music id, so there is
nothing to play directly.

RECORD_AUDIO is requested when the screen opens, and the microphone
feature is declared optional so the app still installs without one.
Leaving the screen releases the microphone and clears the result.

No recognition history yet: that needs a database migration, which is
worth doing on its own rather than inside this.
