From 96e16dce7bc0670ac994374e0a40896d78fe2002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 10:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/46] Position layout blocks by their centre, and allow
 rotation

Schema 3. x and y are now a block's centre rather than its top-left
corner, which is what makes the horizontal control behave the way anyone
would expect: it slides a block across the screen instead of pinning its
left edge, and a centred block stays centred when it is resized.

Done with a translate rather than arithmetic, so text blocks - whose
height nothing knows in advance - centre correctly too.

Cover art is named as such and its free-placement control says Size,
since for a square that is what changing the width does; everything else
still says Width.

Rotation is offered on cover art, the title block and the action row -
the pieces where a tilt reads as deliberate rather than broken.
