Subject: [PATCH 38/46] Colour the queue handle to match the player background

While the queue sheet is collapsed, BottomSheet draws its background at zero
alpha - the fade only starts once the sheet is about a tenth of the way open.
So the handle and the queue title are not on a surface at all: they are sitting
directly on the player background, which with the frosted or blurred styles is
the album art. Painting them onSurface picks a colour for a surface that is not
there, and against a pale cover they disappear.

They now use the same colour the player chose for its own text, which with
automatic contrast on is measured from that very artwork.

The choice itself moved to rememberPlayerOnBackgroundColor, next to the
luminance measurement it depends on, because two places now need the same
answer and working it out separately in each is how they drift apart. It is
unchanged apart from its address. Asking from both costs a second luminance
pass over an 18px bitmap that Coil already has in memory.
