 theme

Lyrics are drawn on top of whatever the player is showing behind them, but they
were painted in the theme's secondary colour, which is chosen to sit on a
surface that is not there. Over a pale album cover with the frosted or blurred
background they were close to unreadable - the same problem the queue handle
had.

They now use the colour measured from that background, which is what the
player's own title and controls already use. With the background set to follow
the theme the measurement is skipped and this resolves to secondary, so nothing
changes for anyone not putting artwork behind the player.

Lines already sung had the same problem for the same reason - the theme's
primary, arbitrary against an album cover - and now take their own shade of the
measured colour instead. That alpha lives in the colour rather than in a
Modifier, so the plain path no longer fades a consumed line a second time on
top of it.
