From d429c1c902e26b0bb0c05f9798201f60900b1166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 02:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/46] Stop the word sweep from silently doing nothing

Three ways it could look dead, all fixed, none of them confirmed as the one -
this is written without a device to reproduce on.

Battery saver was read once with a keyless remember, so it was sampled when the
lyrics were first composed and never again. On a phone that was in battery
saver at that moment the sweep was off for the rest of the session, and turning
battery saver off did not bring it back. Now sampled per song.

The position started at zero and was only written after the frame loop's first
iteration, so the first frame drew a completely unswept line. It is seeded from
the player before the loop begins.

The gate required a current line index, which is -1 until the first tick of the
polling loop; before that no line qualified. The first line now does.

Also, both fallbacks in the renderer - no width, no text, no usable timings -
drew the line at the *unsung* dimness. On the line that is actually playing that
is precisely what a broken sweep looks like, so a provider returning line-level
lyrics was indistinguishable from a rendering fault. They now draw at full
strength, which is also just correct: that line is the one being sung.
