From 3f76d15a3f5cdbc59c4c975cbc9092b579fc7967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 03:58:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] Stop the layout dispatch from changing the built-in
 player

Two faults, both mine, both from making the action row a block.

The action row was drawn twice: once inline beside the song title where it has
always been, and again as a stacked block below the play button, because the
default block list contains ACTIONS and the stack dispatch drew everything in
it. Like and the overflow button appeared in both places. ACTIONS is excluded
from the stack now - there it is inline, and a layout file can only hide it.

And the built-in layout was no longer the built-in layout. The dispatch applied
the imported-layout treatment unconditionally: a 16dp spacer between blocks and
a full-width wrapper around each, neither of which the player had before. With
no file imported there is nothing to apply, so nothing is applied and the
blocks are emitted exactly as they were. This is what made resetting to default
look like it had not worked - it had, and then the dispatch modified the result.

The settings screen also stopped claiming things. Its description was a sticky
message about the last action taken, so it read "Layout reset" or "Imported"
long after that stopped being informative. It now reads the stored layout and
says what is actually in use, which means a reset visibly returns it to the
"import a layout" prompt. Only failures are messages now.
